WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.031 --> 00:00:02.250
(enlightening music)

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.680
- [Narrator] The River
Ganges in Haridwar, India,

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.620
is a holy pilgrimage site
for millions of Hindus

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.400
and is visited by hundreds of
thousands of people each year.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.570
(crowd cheering)

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.789
It's also home to the largest
handwritten family tree

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:17.973
in the world.

00:00:23.432 --> 00:00:24.480
(enlightening music)

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.750
For centuries, a sect of
priests known as Pandits

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.870
have updated and maintained
comprehensive paper records

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:31.743
on each visitor.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:03.220
- [Narrator] Each of
the records are sorted

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.430
by family lineage and
include reports of births,

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:08.670
deaths and other important events,

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.983
many of which span hundreds of years.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.360
- [Narrator] While talks
are underway to digitize

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.930
these records, the Pandits take great care

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:41.040
to preserve each delicate
page in hopes of maintaining

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.433
family histories for generations to come.

